{"name":"Cattail Red","hex":"#b64925","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cattail","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of several perennial herbs, of the genus Typha, that have long flat leaves, and grow in marshy places.","A cat-o'-nine-tails."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cattail"},{"term":"red","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of the setting sun, blood, and strawberries; the color which is evoked by the longest visible wavelengths (between about 625–740 nm), and a primary additive color.","A revolutionary socialist or (most commonly) a Communist;  a Bolshevik, a supporter of the Bolsheviks in the Russian Civil War."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a red hue.","Having an orange-brown or orange-blond colour; ginger."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/red"}],"entries":[{"title":"Typha","blocks":[{"text":"Typha is a genus of about 30 species of monocotyledonous flowering plants in the family Typhaceae. These plants have a variety of common names, in British English bulrush or reedmace, in American English cattail or punks, in Australia cumbungi or bulrush, in Canada bulrush or cattail, and in New Zealand raupō, bullrush, cattail, or reed."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/59/Typha-cattails-in-indiana.jpg/330px-Typha-cattails-in-indiana.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Typha","wikidata":"Q145707"},{"title":"Red","blocks":[{"text":"Red is the color at the long wavelength end of the visible spectrum of light, next to orange and opposite violet. It has a dominant wavelength of approximately 625–750 nanometers. It is a primary color in the RGB color model and a secondary color in the CMYK color model, and is the complementary color of cyan. Reds range from the brilliant yellow-tinged scarlet and vermillion to bluish-red crimson, and vary in shade from the pale red pink to the dark red burgundy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg/330px-Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red","wikidata":"Q3142"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/2022-07-26_10_59_59_A_Broadleaf_Cattail_along_a_small_tributary_of_the_Delaware_River_adjacent_to_New_Jersey_State_Route_29_%28River_Road%29_in_the_Mountainview_section_of_Ewing_Township%2C_Mercer_County%2C_New_Jersey.jpg/250px-thumbnail.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/2022-07-26_10_59_59_A_Broadleaf_Cattail_along_a_small_tributary_of_the_Delaware_River_adjacent_to_New_Jersey_State_Route_29_%28River_Road%29_in_the_Mountainview_section_of_Ewing_Township%2C_Mercer_County%2C_New_Jersey.jpg/500px-thumbnail.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/2022-07-26_10_59_59_A_Broadleaf_Cattail_along_a_small_tributary_of_the_Delaware_River_adjacent_to_New_Jersey_State_Route_29_%28River_Road%29_in_the_Mountainview_section_of_Ewing_Township%2C_Mercer_County%2C_New_Jersey.jpg/250px-thumbnail.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A2022-07-26_10_59_59_A_Broadleaf_Cattail_along_a_small_tributary_of_the_Delaware_River_adjacent_to_New_Jersey_State_Route_29_(River_Road)_in_the_Mountainview_section_of_Ewing_Township%2C_Mercer_County%2C_New_Jersey.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Going_bald_%2832413540641%29.jpg/250px-Going_bald_%2832413540641%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/